HST Office: ribbon groups take room back in their ladder's growth order; menu buttons shrink.

- vcl/inc/HstRibbonRegrow.hxx: fitByPriority() takes an optional growth order (growthOrder()): the least
  used groups still collapse first, the shown ones grow back in that order. HstRibbonLadders.hxx lists
  it per ladder (ladders::growths, generate-ribbon-priorities.py): Sheets' Home gives the room to Editing,
  Cells and Styles before Font, so Font gives up its labels first and still collapses last.
- vcl/source/control/PriorityMergedHBox.cxx: reads the growth order of the tab's ladder and passes it to
  every fitByPriority() call (the row, the groups left beside the chevron, the block-beside check).
- vcl/source/control/HstRibbonLadder.cxx: the menu buttons of a group with an image drop their label at the
  small state, as the toolboxes do (label kept as accessible name and tooltip). Groups made of menu
  buttons (Sheets' Cells and Editing) kept their full width down to the small state, so the ladder
  collapsed them while groups of toolboxes beside them kept their labels.

